      "content": "it's a good start, but i feel like the activist's side is sounding a bit too weak/uninformed here. can we refine it? i want the senator to come across as the voice of reason—using really tight, structured logic about national security and the necessity of data—while the activist stays high-energy and emotional, but their arguments should feel a bit scattered and less coherent so the senator can easily shut them down.",
